! transmit_time_to_index.strap -- a TRANSMIT's time is set by where the
! words GO (docs/fidelity_plan.md A7, 2026-11-27).
!
! FIVE WORDS FROM CORE TO INDEX STORAGE ($2-$6, words 18-22), immediate
! count.  Perf. Char. Vol. 1 Table 9 (printed p.3-14, PDF 32), T (EM ->
! XS): loop 4.2 us = 14 clocks a word; Vol. 2 PDF 107 (printed 100)
! measures EXTERNAL TO I-BOX at 14.06.  The model charged the SOURCE read
! until A7: about 10 clocks a word from core.  The sibling is
! transmit_time_to_core.strap, whose header has the argument.
!
! THE CYCLES PIN (tests/run_tests.sh) is the model's count for the whole
! deck, a model pin.  The transmit's part is bsv/StretchXmitTiming.bsv's
! charge, F + 5 L with F = 30 (TI into index storage) and L = 14.
! Injections and their observed results are in run_tests.sh at the run.

        SLC, (8)2000.0
START   TI, 5, SRC, 18.0         ! SRC..SRC+4 to $2-$6
        BEW, $

        SLC, (8)3000.0
SRC     DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000011
        DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000022
        DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000033
        DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000044
        DD(BU,64), (16)0000000000000055

        END, START
